{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1153223-custom-endowment-1st-ed-question","id":1153223,"title":"Custom endowment (1st ed) question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-26T10:41:44-07:00","id":1153223,"title":"Custom endowment (1st ed) question","content":"A player is introducing a power and we are looking for some wisdom. The question of whether the entity should contest with:<br /> <br /> Wits + Occult vs....<br /> <br /> Permanent willpower (Resolve + Composure)<br /> Resolve + Tolerance<br /> <br /> The power makes it so that dread powers cannot activate for X turns (rough draft right now). The question is an issue of design: how do you all make a judgment when designing endowments and their resisted/contested pools? Most often, the single resistance trait + Tolerance seems to be the obvious choice as examples set forth in the rule book, but some endowments are contested by willpower. What makes you choose one or the other when making yours? (consider the Awe numina)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12209-adonus","name":"adonus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}